data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:22:24.081458+00:00", "content": "Based on my investigation of **ce_branch24**, here is the comprehensive status report with all cited evidence.\n\n---\n\n### **Device Overview**\n**ce_branch24** is a branch-office SD-WAN edge device (site_type=branch, agent_host=172.20.20.160) with **6 active tunnels** to hubs **ce_hub1\u2013ce_hub6** across **CORP** and **VOICE** VRFs [topo:ce_branch24]. All SD-WAN paths report `sdwan_path_active=1` [metrics:82][metrics:83].\n\n---\n\n### **SD-WAN Tunnel Health (per-hub, latest sample)**\n\n| Hub | Latency (ms) | Jitter (ms) | Loss (%) | Rekeys (total) |\n|-----|--------------|-------------|----------|----------------|\n| ce_hub1 | 72.6 [metrics:90] | 2.5 [metrics:84] | **0.94** [metrics:96] | 5 [metrics:102] |\n| ce_hub2 | 63.2 [metrics:91] | **1.3** [metrics:85] | 0.18 [metrics:97] | **21** [metrics:103] |\n| ce_hub3 | 69.8 [metrics:92] | 6.0 [metrics:86] | 0.07 [metrics:98] | **25** [metrics:104] |\n| ce_hub4 | 66.0 [metrics:93] | 6.1 [metrics:87] | 0.10 [metrics:99] | 4 [metrics:105] |\n| ce_hub5 | 63.1 [metrics:94] | **8.2** [metrics:88] | 0.13 [metrics:100] | 4 [metrics:106] |\n| ce_hub6 | 70.6 [metrics:95] | 7.7 [metrics:89] | **0.02** [metrics:101] | 4 [metrics:107] |\n\n**Key observations:**\n- **ce_hub1** shows the highest loss (0.94%) and highest latency (72.6 ms) [metrics:90][metrics:96].\n- **ce_hub2** and **ce_hub3** have **high rekey counts (21, 25)** vs. 4\u20135 on others [metrics:103][metrics:104], suggesting possible tunnel flapping or key-rotation storms.\n- **ce_hub5** has the highest jitter (8.2 ms) [metrics:88]; **ce_hub6** the lowest loss (0.02%) [metrics:101].\n\n---\n\n### **Interface & Traffic Profile**\n\n| Interface | In (octets) | Out (octets) | In-Discards | Out-Discards | Queue Drops | OperStatus |\n|-----------|-------------|--------------|-------------|--------------|-------------|------------|\n| eth0 (WAN?) | 9.9 M [metrics:8] | 3.8 M [metrics:17] | **1,877** [metrics:26] | 0 | **91** [metrics:6] | Up [metrics:53] |\n| eth1 | 105 K [metrics:9] | 80 K [metrics:18] | 0 | 0 | 2 [metrics:7] | Up [metrics:54] |\n| eth2 | 1.7 K [metrics:10] | 1.8 K [metrics:19] | 0 | 0 | 0 | Up [metrics:55] |\n| eth3 | 103 K [metrics:11] | 85 K [metrics:20] | 0 | 0 | 0 | Up [metrics:56] |\n| eth4 | 1.7 K [metrics:12] | 1.7 K [metrics:21] | 0 | 0 | 0 | Up [metrics:57] |\n| wg0 (WireGuard) | 941 K [metrics:16] | 963 K [metrics:25] | 0 | **4** [metrics:70] | 0 | Up [metrics:61] |\n| vrf_CORP | 56 K [metrics:14] | **0** [metrics:23] | 0 | 0 | 0 | Up [metrics:59] |\n| vrf_VOICE | 54 K [metrics:15] | **0** [metrics:24] | 0 | 0 | 0 | Up [metrics:60] |\n\n**Concerns:**\n- **eth0** has **1,877 in-discards** and **91 queue drops** [metrics:26][metrics:6] \u2014 possible congestion or MTU mismatch on the WAN uplink.\n- **vrf_CORP** and **vrf_VOICE** show inbound traffic but **zero outbound** [metrics:23][metrics:24] \u2014 verify asymmetric routing or egress policy.\n- **wg0** has 4 out-discards [metrics:70] \u2014 minimal but worth tracking.\n\n---\n\n### **Hardware & System Health**\n- **Fan:** 3,000 RPM [metrics:0] \u2014 normal.\n- **Power:** 69.2 W [metrics:1], **PSU:** 11.9 V [metrics:2] \u2014 within spec.\n- **Chassis Temp:** 29.0 \u00b0C [metrics:3], **XCVR (eth1) Temp:** 37.2 \u00b0C [metrics:109] \u2014 healthy.\n- **XCVR (eth1) RX Power:** \u20135.8 dBm [metrics:108], **TX Bias:** 28.3 mA [metrics:110] \u2014 good optical margin.\n- **CPU:** 0.4 % [metrics:80], **Memory:** 0.19 % [metrics:81] \u2014 idle.\n\n---\n\n### **Topology & Blast Radius**\n- **Hop-0:** ce_branch24 (this device) [topo:ce_branch24]\n- **Hop-1:** h_branch24_corp, h_branch24_voice (local hubs, no metrics), **pe12** (provider edge, healthy: BGP established=2, MPLS LSPs=113, OSPF neighbor=Full) [topo:pe12]\n- **Hop-2:** ce_branch12 (peer branch, loss 2.6% on its tunnel [topo:ce_branch12]), p23, p24 (core P-routers, healthy) [topo:p23][topo:p24]\n\nNo downstream devices show critical alarms; pe12 and core P-routers are clean.\n\n---\n\n### **Logs & Flows**\n- **search_logs:** No log entries returned for the window [events: none].\n- **flows:** No flow records returned [flows: none].\n\n---\n\n### **Runbooks & Past Incidents**\n- `search_runbooks` and `search_incidents` backends returned **unavailable** \u2014 unable to retrieve procedural guidance or historical matches at this time.\n\n---\n\n### **Action Items for System Administrator (Full Override Authority)**\n\n1. **Investigate ce_hub2 / ce_hub3 tunnel rekeys (21 / 25)** \u2014 capture tunnel flap logs on both ends; check IKE/IPsec lifetime mismatches or DPD timers.\n2. **Diagnose ce_hub1 loss (0.94%)** \u2014 run synthetic probes (TWAMP/BFD) on that path; verify underlay path MTU and QoS markings.\n3. **Clear eth0 in-discards / queue drops** \u2014 check for duplex/speed mismatch, policing, or MTU mismatch on the WAN interface; consider raising queue depth or shaping.\n4. **Validate vrf_CORP / vrf_VOICE egress** \u2014 confirm route-maps / PBR allow outbound traffic; verify hub-side return paths.\n5. **Monitor ce_hub5 jitter (8.2 ms)** \u2014 if sustained, consider shifting primary traffic to lower-jitter tunnels (ce_hub2, ce_hub4).\n6. **Enable ranged metric collection** on `sdwan_tunnel_latency_ms`, `jitter_ms`, `loss_pct` for trend analysis (Grafana dashboards per #56).\n\nAll above findings are grounded in live telemetry captured within the investigation window. Let me know if you want deeper trend series (ranged=true) on any specific tunnel or interface."}

